      "census_id": "W-SSC-031",
      "unit": "W01",
      "frozen_obligation_exact": "For a torsion-free connection W01 states the vacuum Einstein condition as vanishing of a specified mixed/chiral curvature component and motivates a chiral formulation using only the right-handed connection/curvature sector; the omitted left connection becomes unconstrained if torsion is allowed. W01's exact torsion-free vacuum Einstein condition is Omega_(-,R)(omega)=0, and W01 separately prints its implication Omega_(+,L)(omega)=0. A third distinct source statement says solutions with Omega_(-,L)=0 will be self-dual/half-flat. These are not three interchangeable vanishing conditions and the first is conditional on torsion freedom. Chiral gravitational action replaces Omega by Omega_R, with the omitted omega_L left unconstrained only if torsion is allowed.",
